From 9935660117f63aa2c0bad89430e3e6b16cd191d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ttyS3 <41882455+ttys3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 08:53:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat: support the Program Status Protocol (OSC 7501)

Implement revision 0.4 of the Program Status Protocol, which lets a
program report whether it is idle, working, done, blocked on the user
or failed, and why.

- Parse and validate reports per the spec: limits, base64 text without
  control characters, malformed ids discard the report instead of
  falling back to the root record, unknown states are ignored
- Keep up to 256 records per window (LRU eviction), with clear removing
  a record and its descendants and app inherited from ancestors
- Reply to the feature detection query with supported states and kinds
- Lifetime: working/blocked/idle records are dropped at a new shell
  prompt (OSC 133;A), done/error are dropped when the window gets focus,
  a full reset (RIS) removes every record
- Expose records via tab.program_status in tab_title_template, the
  output of kitten @ ls and a new on_program_status_change watcher

Spec: https://www.superlogical.com/rex/docs/build/program-status
Ref: ghostty-org/ghostty#14560, ghostty-org/ghostty#14630

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
